{
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5,
  "metadata": {
    "kernelspec": {
      "name": "maxima",
      "display_name": "Maxima",
      "language": "maxima"
    },
    "aximar": {}
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# The Complex Plane\n\nA complex number is $z = x + iy$ with $x, y \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and $i^2 = -1$. As a set, $\\mathbb{C}$ is identified with $\\mathbb{R}^2$ via $z \\leftrightarrow (x, y)$. What's new is the **multiplication**: $(a + ib)(c + id) = (ac - bd) + i(ad + bc)$, which gives $\\mathbb{C}$ the structure of a field.\n\nGeometric incarnation: in **polar form** $z = r e^{i\\theta}$ with $r = |z|$ and $\\theta = \\arg z$, multiplication multiplies the moduli and adds the arguments:\n\n$$z_1 z_2 = r_1 r_2 e^{i(\\theta_1 + \\theta_2)}.$$\n\nMultiplication is **rotation + scaling**. That single fact distinguishes complex analysis from real $\\mathbb{R}^2$ analysis — and underpins everything that follows.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Modulus and argument [S+N]\n\nMaxima knows complex numbers natively.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "z : 3 + 4*%i$\nprint(\"z =\", z)$\nprint(\"|z| =\", float(cabs(z)))$\nprint(\"arg z =\", float(carg(z)), \"rad =\", float(carg(z)) * 180 / float(%pi), \"deg\")$\nprint(\"Re z =\", realpart(z), \"  Im z =\", imagpart(z))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "z = 4*%i+3\n|z| = 5.0\narg z = 0.9272952180016122 rad = 53.13010235415598 deg\nRe z = 3   Im z = 4"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Multiplication as rotation + scaling\n\nMultiplying by $i$ rotates by $90°$. Multiplying by $\\sqrt{2}\\,e^{i\\pi/4} = 1 + i$ scales by $\\sqrt{2}$ and rotates by $45°$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "z0 : 2 + %i$\nmul_factors : [%i, 1 + %i, 1 + 2*%i]$\nproducts : map(lambda([w], expand(z0 * w)), mul_factors)$\nprint(\"z₀ =\", z0)$\nfor k : 1 thru length(mul_factors) do\n  print(\"z₀ ·\", mul_factors[k], \"=\", products[k],\n        \"  (|·| =\", float(cabs(products[k])),\n        \", arg =\", float(carg(products[k])) * 180 / float(%pi), \"°)\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "z₀ = %i+2\nz₀ · %i = 2*%i-1   (|·| = 2.23606797749979 , arg = 116.56505117707799 °)\nz₀ · %i+1 = 3*%i+1   (|·| = 3.1622776601683795 , arg = 71.56505117707799 °)\nz₀ · 2*%i+1 = 5*%i   (|·| = 5.0 , arg = 90.0 °)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Plot a few points and their products\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "points_re : [float(realpart(z0))]$\npoints_im : [float(imagpart(z0))]$\nfor p in products do (\n  points_re : endcons(float(realpart(p)), points_re),\n  points_im : endcons(float(imagpart(p)), points_im))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  marker_size=12, color=\"red\", name=\"z₀ = 2 + i\",\n  points([float(realpart(z0))], [float(imagpart(z0))]),\n  marker_size=10, color=\"blue\", name=\"z₀ · (i, 1+i, 1+2i)\",\n  points(rest(points_re), rest(points_im)),\n  color=\"black\", dash=\"dot\", explicit(0, t, -10, 10),\n  title=\"Complex multiplication = rotate + scale\",\n  xlabel=\"Re\", ylabel=\"Im\",\n  grid=true, aspect_ratio=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": [
        {
