    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Polar form and roots of unity\n\nThe **n-th roots of unity** are $e^{2\\pi i k/n}$ for $k = 0, 1, \\ldots, n-1$. They sit on the unit circle at equally-spaced angles. Plot for $n = 7$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "n_roots : 7$\nangles : makelist(2 * float(%pi) * k / n_roots, k, 0, n_roots - 1)$\nroots_re : map(cos, angles)$\nroots_im : map(sin, angles)$\n\ntheta_grid : np_to_list(np_linspace(0, 2*float(%pi), 100))$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"lightgrey\", line_width=1, name=\"unit circle\",\n  lines(map(cos, theta_grid), map(sin, theta_grid)),\n  marker_size=10, color=\"red\", name=\"7th roots of unity\",\n  points(roots_re, roots_im),\n  title=\"z⁷ = 1 has seven solutions on the unit circle\",\n  xlabel=\"Re\", ylabel=\"Im\",\n  grid=true, aspect_ratio=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
